# hardware.rst: how an edge is made and measured (irq_latency, wrapped ISR).
# Schematic: 1 unit is 1 pixel; the box widths fit the labels, they are
# not durations. The masks are those of the pinned trees (both the same).
include apps.tdc
diagram stim-method "One edge: stim_arm() programs the compare value, the hardware makes the edge, the ISR reads the counter"
schematic

piece "stim_arm(now) in the ISR of the previous edge" 0..382
break "random delay"
dev 36 "now" : The ISR read the counter (now = stim_now()) as its first action.
dev 43 "next" : stim_arm(now) adds a random delay to now: the time of the next edge. Interrupts are not locked yet.
dev 56 "checks" {basepri} : irq_lock() sets BASEPRI. A fresh count of the stimulus timer and of the system timer. If the edge is less than 1000 counts after the fresh count, it moves to 1000 counts after it (stim_late). The tick phase of the edge.
dev 115 "port_stim_set()" {basepri} : Pin low (forced inactive), the edge time into the compare register, clear the compare flag, then "active on match". Then irq_unlock().
dev 43 "exit" : The ISR exit. No thread is ready, so there is no PendSV.
idle 49 "idle" {basepri} : The idle loop: arch_irq_lock() sets BASEPRI. Then k_cpu_idle() sets PRIMASK and clears BASEPRI.
@sleeps anchor
idle sleep sleeps..382 "WFI" {primask} : WFI with PRIMASK set.

piece "after the edge" -30..313
@edge "edge: CNT = compare value"
hw 76 "pin, NVIC" : The timer drives the stimulus pin high. The wire takes the edge to the response pin. EXTI detects it, and the NVIC makes the interrupt pending. The pending interrupt wakes the core.
@pending anchor
idle sleep -30..pending "WFI" {primask} : The idle thread sleeps in WFI with PRIMASK set. The stimulus timer counts on.
idle 49 "cpsie" {primask} : The idle thread clears PRIMASK (cpsie i, in k_cpu_idle()). Only then can the interrupt start.
hw 49 "entry" : Exception entry: register stacking and vector fetch.
dev 60 "wrapper" : _isr_wrapper (the wrapped path only). It does not lock interrupts.
dev 36 "now" : The first action of the ISR reads the counter: now = stim_now().
@stamp "stim_now()"
dev 43 "hist" : on_edge(): the histogram, then stim_arm(now) for the next edge, as in the left part.
span edge..stamp "stim_now() - stim_edge()" !
